Hey there! We are observing flaky tests related to hovering and I was able to create an example to reproduce it. It's probably not related but it's kind of similar to [this one](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/issues/27475), as it only seems to be happening in `headed` mode. This time, it's affecting all browsers and it's also a bit less likely to happen.

### System info
- Playwright Version: v1.38.1
- Operating System: Ubuntu 22, MacOS Ventura 13.3.1
- Browser: All
- Other info: I tested this in docker with the latest official docker image `mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.38.1` as well as locally on macOS Ventura 13.3.1.

### Source code

- [x] I provided exact source code that allows reproducing the issue locally.

**Config file**

```ts
// playwright.config.ts
import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  workers: 2,
  projects: [
   {
      name: "chromium",
      use: { ...devices["Desktop Chrome"] },
    },
    {
      name: "firefox",
      use: { ...devices["Desktop Firefox"] },
    },
    {
      name: "webkit",
      use: { ...devices["Desktop Safari"] },
    },
  ]
});
```

**Test file (self-contained)**
This mimics one of our tests. We have a card that reveals a button when the card is hovered, however with a slight delay. 

```ts
test("keeps the hover state", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.setContent(`
  <div data-testid="container" class="container">
    <div>test</div>
    <button type="button">click me</button>
  </div>
 `);

  await page.addStyleTag({
    content: `
    .container {
      position: relative;
      width: 100px;
      height: 100px;
    }

    button {
      display: none;
      position: absolute;
      top: 0;
      right: 0;
    }

    .container:hover button {
      display: block;
    }
  `,
  });
  await page.getByTestId("container").hover();
  
  // even after the timeout, the button should be visible and clickable
  await page.waitForTimeout(1000);

  await page.getByRole("button", { name: "click me" }).click();
});
```

**Steps**
- Start the docker container `docker run --rm --network host -v $(pwd):/work/ -w /work/ -it mcr.microsoft.com/playwright:v1.38.1 /bin/bash`
- Run `xvfb-run npx playwright test --project chromium --headed --repeat-each 20`

**Expected**
- Tests using hover are not flaky when running them with multiple workers in headed mode

**Actual**
Running the above will always have some failing tests for me:

<img width="825" alt="CleanShot 2023-10-09 at 22 24 06@2x" src="https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/assets/4624537/5d4329b4-34f0-4ab0-ab19-6ac80991ede7">

It won't happen in `headless` mode and it also won't happen if I add `--workers 1`. It happens in webkit and firefox as well, however it seems less likely there (I need to repeat them more often to get to failing tests). It also happens outside of docker in macOS. 

Let me know if you need more information, thanks in advance.
